title E-commerce on AWS
direction right

Shopper [icon: user]
Admin [icon: admin]
Route 53 [icon: aws-route53]
CloudFront [icon: aws-cloudfront, color: purple]
WAF [icon: aws-waf, color: red]

AWS Cloud [icon: aws-cloud, color: orange] {
  VPC [icon: aws-vpc, color: green, description: 10.0.0.0/16] {
    Public subnet [color: green, description: 10.0.1.0/24] {
      ALB [icon: aws-elb]
      NAT gateway [icon: aws-vpc]
    }
    App subnet [color: blue, description: 10.0.2.0/24] {
      Storefront [icon: aws-ecs, description: ECS Fargate]
      Catalog [icon: aws-ecs, description: ECS Fargate]
      Checkout [icon: aws-ecs, description: ECS Fargate]
      Search [icon: aws-opensearch]
    }
    Data subnet [color: purple, description: 10.0.3.0/24] {
      Orders DB [icon: aws-rds, description: Aurora Postgres]
      Cache [icon: aws-elasticache, description: Redis]
    }
  }
  Product images [icon: aws-s3]
  Order events [icon: aws-sqs]
  Fulfillment [icon: aws-lambda]
  Emails [icon: aws-ses]
}
Payment provider [icon: stripe]
Warehouse API [icon: warehouse]

Shopper > Route 53 > CloudFront > WAF > ALB
Admin > ALB: admin console
ALB > Storefront, Catalog, Checkout
Storefront > Catalog, Search
Catalog > Orders DB, Cache
Catalog > Product images
Checkout > Orders DB
Checkout > Payment provider: charge [color: green]
Checkout --> Order events: OrderCreated
Order events > Fulfillment
Fulfillment > Warehouse API, Emails
App subnet > NAT gateway: outbound
